Electronic Samurai wrote:
> Right now I'm playing an elf ranger who's been polymorphed into an
> Aleax since the Castle, and I'm nearing the Ascension.  I've raised my
> HP to over 300 using nurses and !oFH, and I have a chest full of rings
> and amulets back in Orcus' town.  I was considering polymorphing into a
> Xorn to see what I could eat for intrinsics, but I'm worried if
> anything will happen to the health I've gained.
> 
> Will the HPs remain when I unpolymorph to elf?  How about when I repoly
> into a Xorn?  Or, finally, when I go back to Aleax?
> 

You lose the statistics of your polymorphed form when you unpoly. So 
when you lose your Aleax form, you lose the effects of your !oFH and any 
!oGain Ability, etc. This is consistent with the fact that you can't 
permanently gain constitution by eating a ring of gain constitution, as 
you just lose the stat when you unpoly.

That said, the stats of your natural form (elf) ARE remembered between 
polymorphs. The only exception is when you "Feel like a new Elf" and 
your stats get randomly adjusted a bit; even still, they don't get reset.

When you poly into any form, even a form you've been before, you get the 
basic stats of that creature. That means that your Xorn form will likely 
have very few (sub-100) hitpoints. It's usually not a problem because 
running out of hitpoints just turns you back into your elf form, where 
you probably have a few hundred hp more.

